{"id":"a5","level":2,"levelName":"Ulpan Alef","n":6,"of":19,"title":"Adjectives agree","titleHe":"שֵׁם תֹּאַר","goal":"Put an adjective after its noun and match it in gender, number and definiteness.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"An adjective comes after the noun it describes, not before, and it copies three things from it: gender, number, and whether it has the article."},{"type":"table","caption":"גָּדוֹל — big","head":["","singular","plural"],"rows":[["masculine","יֶלֶד גָּדוֹל","יְלָדִים גְּדוֹלִים"],["feminine","יַלְדָּה גְּדוֹלָה","יְלָדוֹת גְּדוֹלוֹת"]]},{"type":"tip","body":"If the noun takes the article, so does the adjective: הַיֶּלֶד הַגָּדוֹל, the big boy. Leave the second הַ off and you've written a whole sentence instead — הַיֶּלֶד גָּדוֹל means the boy is big."},{"type":"text","body":"The endings are the same ones nouns take, so there is nothing new to learn — only the habit of writing them twice. Here are the commonest adjectives in all four forms."},{"type":"table","caption":"Four forms apiece","head":["masculine","feminine","m. plural","f. plural"],"rows":[["גָּדוֹל — big","גְּדוֹלָה","גְּדוֹלִים","גְּדוֹלוֹת"],["קָטָן — small","קְטַנָּה","קְטַנִּים","קְטַנּוֹת"],["טוֹב — good","טוֹבָה","טוֹבִים","טוֹבוֹת"],["חָדָשׁ — new","חֲדָשָׁה","חֲדָשִׁים","חֲדָשׁוֹת"],["יָפֶה — beautiful","יָפָה","יָפִים","יָפוֹת"],["קָשֶׁה — difficult","קָשָׁה","קָשִׁים","קָשׁוֹת"]]}],"vocab":[{"he":"גָּדוֹל","en":"big","translit":"gadol"},{"he":"קָטָן","en":"small","translit":"katan"},{"he":"טוֹב","en":"good","translit":"tov"},{"he":"רַע","en":"bad","translit":"ra"},{"he":"יָפֶה","en":"beautiful","translit":"yafe"},{"he":"חָדָשׁ","en":"new","translit":"chadash"},{"he":"יָשָׁן","en":"old (of things)","translit":"yashan"},{"he":"קָשֶׁה","en":"hard, difficult","translit":"kashe"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["receives, gets","wine","big","chicken, fowl"],"correct":2,"prompt":"גָּדוֹל","translit":"gadol"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["narrative, legend","it's possible","knife","small"],"correct":3,"prompt":"קָטָן","translit":"katan"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["at most","good","mum","late"],"correct":1,"prompt":"טוֹב","translit":"tov"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["ant","bad","cucumber","excuse me, sorry"],"correct":1,"prompt":"רַע","translit":"ra"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["while","beautiful","morals, rebuke","open"],"correct":1,"prompt":"יָפֶה","translit":"yafe"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["young","new","teacher (m.)","sadness"],"correct":1,"prompt":"חָדָשׁ","translit":"chadash"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["stops","not yet","balcony","old (of things)"],"correct":3,"prompt":"יָשָׁן","translit":"yashan"},{"type":"read","he":"קָטָן","translit":"katan","en":"small"},{"type":"choice","q":"Four forms apiece — big?","options":["חֲדָשׁוֹת","טוֹבוֹת","קְטַנּוֹת","גְּדוֹלוֹת"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"“The big house” is —","options":["הַבַּיִת הַגָּדוֹל","הַבַּיִת גָּדוֹל","בַּיִת הַגָּדוֹל","הַגָּדוֹל הַבַּיִת"],"correct":0,"why":"Both words take the article. Without the second one, הַבַּיִת גָּדוֹל, you've said the house is big."},{"type":"choice","q":"Four forms apiece — new?","options":["גְּדוֹלוֹת","קְטַנּוֹת","טוֹבוֹת","חֲדָשׁוֹת"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"What does הַיַּלְדָּה קְטַנָּה mean?","options":["The girl is small","The small girl","A small girl","The girl and the small one"],"correct":0,"why":"The adjective has no article, so this is a sentence, not a phrase."},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “old (of things)”?","options":["יָשָׁן","דֹּב","עָיֵף","שׁוֹמֵעַ"],"correct":0,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “new”?","options":["חָדָשׁ","חֶמְאָה","בָּרוּר","מַפְתֵּחַ"],"correct":0,"he":true},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["טוֹב","קָשֶׁה","רַע","גָּדוֹל"],"correct":2,"say":"רַע","he":true},{"type":"type","q":"Write “beautiful” in Hebrew","answer":"יָפֶה","hint":"yafe"}]}